WIRED magazine's new online service @WIRED is proud to announce our
creative team leaders: 

o Howard Rheingold
o Chip Bayers
o Barbara Kuhr

All of us at WIRED magazine and @WIRED are extremely excited by the depth
and excitement our new creative team brings to our forthcoming online
service. @WIRED, which will launch later this year, will not be a linear
extension of the magazine, but new content for a new medium. Our creative
team's mission is to shape that content and engage the imaginations and
energy of the online community. (Stay tuned for further details, and the
launch date.) 


Editor/Author/Visionary Howard Rheingold is one of the best-known and
sharpest authorities on electronically-mediated communities in the world.
His latest book, "The Virtual Community" (Addison/Wesley, 1993), is widely
regarded as the best analysis of this global phenomenon. Rheingold is an
accomplished writer, speaker, editor (former Whole Earth Review
editor-in-chief), Net personality, and all around visionary - and @WIRED is
proud to announce his addition to our creative team. 

"Once a generation, a few people have the opportunity to shape a new
medium," says Rheingold. "I can remember how excited I was when I first
used a computer as a writing tool, when I first plugged my computer into my
telephone and discovered the Net, and when I first saw Mosaic. I see an
opportunity to create a new role as information arbiter/artist. We have the
opportunity to pick up the Net, like the first rock-and-rollers picked up
electric guitars, and make this new medium DANCE!" 


Chip Bayers comes to @WIRED from his position as Senior Editor at Michael
Wolff & Company, NYC. He is co-author of the highly acclaimed "Net Guide -
What's On in Cyberspace" (Random House, 1994). 

"It's a thrill for me to be joining the team at such an exciting time in
the growth of the Net and net media," says Bayers. "WIRED, our print
parent, has already established a family tradition of award-winning
excellence. With those genes, I know we can extend that tradition to
@WIRED. We'll be creating content and context with the same authority and
verve you've come to expect from WIRED, while establishing our own unique
personality and perspective." 


Barbara Kuhr is a partner in Plunkett + Kuhr, the design firm responsible
for the look and feel of WIRED. Barbara and John Plunkett started working
with Louis Rossetto and Jane Metcalfe in 1990 to create WIRED magazine.
John continues to act as the creative director, while Barbara acts as the
opinionated "shadowy presence." Now, Barbara turns her focus towards the
creation of @WIRED. Other Plunkett + Kuhr projects include exhibits for
Carnegie Hall and graphics for the Sundance Film Festival. Their work has
received recognition from the American Institute of Graphic Arts, the
Industrial Designers Society of America, and the Society of Environmental
Graphic Designers. 

"I'm incredibly excited," says Kuhr. "It's 1948, and television has just
begun to penetrate the mass market. We are at the birth of a new medium.
I'm looking forward to collaborating with Howard and Chip, plus the rest of
the @WIRED crew and all our contributors, to help shape the future of
media." 


